WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV v3.0 — eco-knowledge (90s) Narrator Julius

1
00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:07.259
First, claims without timestamps and sources go stale fast and let copied summaries fake consensus.

2
00:00:07.759 --> 00:00:15.913
Second, every claim records valid time, write time, frame, scale, scope, certainty, and source lineage.

3
00:00:16.413 --> 00:00:24.188
Third, checking mathematical proofs across six independent Lean proof kernels removes single-compiler blind spots completely.

4
00:00:24.688 --> 00:00:29.781
A patient blood-pressure reading from Tuesday and a tax rate from nineteen ninety-eight

5
00:00:29.781 --> 00:00:34.522
are both genuine facts that turn into costly errors once stripped of dates. Worse

6
00:00:34.522 --> 00:00:41.371
yet, automated summaries routinely cite secondary summaries until unverified guesses look like established consensus.

7
00:00:41.871 --> 00:00:46.738
On knowledge dot openie dot dev, no statement floats bare in memory. Every

8
00:00:46.738 --> 00:00:52.854
recorded claim stores valid world time, ledger write time, reference clock frame, measurement

9
00:00:52.854 --> 00:00:59.037
scale, explicit boundary scope, certainty level, and a directed graph back to primary sources.

10
00:00:59.537 --> 00:01:04.393
For mathematical statements, proof dot openie dot dev checks formal derivations in

11
00:01:04.393 --> 00:01:09.545
Lean four point three six across six independently written proof kernels—verifying five

12
00:01:09.545 --> 00:01:15.230
thousand four hundred ninety-six theorem constants with zero skipped proofs or opaque shortcuts.

13
00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:21.060
Keeping dated physical sensor readings, simulation runs, open scientific hypotheses,

14
00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:28.928
and six-kernel mathematical proofs visibly separate lets humans and machines build reliable knowledge on trustworthy ground.
